arguments.content:
💡 **SUGGESTION: this probe can throw the exact error class this PR fixes in install.ps1**

If `LOCALAPPDATA` is unset **and** `USERPROFILE` is also unset, `Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE 'AppData\Local'` is a terminating parameter-binding error (`Cannot bind argument to parameter 'Path' because it is null`) — the very failure mode this PR fixes in `install.ps1`, which layers `[Environment]::GetFolderPath(...)` → `$env:USERPROFILE` → an explicit, clearly-worded fatal `throw`.

A shell with neither variable is much rarer than one missing only `LOCALAPPDATA` (that's why this is a suggestion, not a must-fix), but the asymmetry is easy to close by reusing the same resolution the installer performs — e.g.:

```powershell
$faLocalRoot = if ($env:LOCALAPPDATA) { $env:LOCALAPPDATA }
               elseif ($env:USERPROFILE) { Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE 'AppData\Local' }
               else { [Environment]::GetFolderPath('LocalApplicationData') }
if (-not $faLocalRoot) { throw "cannot resolve LOCALAPPDATA/USERPROFILE - set it, then rerun the wizard." }
```

For context (unchanged code, outside this diff): line 28 `$FahConfigDir = Join-Path $env:USERPROFILE ".fah"` has the same exposure and predates this PR — worth a follow-up if the wizard is ever hardened the same way.
